<title>USA: Maine to run more advertisements to boost tourism.</title>
<headline>Maine to run more advertisements to boost tourism.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>A new advertizing campaign aimed at bringing more tourists to Maine will start appearing this spring in several magazines.</p>
<p>Economic Development Commissioner Tom McBreaity says $600,000 will be spent on ads in such magazines as Time and Newsweek.</p>
<p>McBreaity says he would like to use television advertising, but his budget does not allow for it.</p>
<p>He says if lawmakers increase his advertising budget, he can bring more tourists to the state and bolster state revenues.</p>
<p>((--Joan Gralla, 212-859-1654))</p>
